  :claim/project :project/aiueos,
  :claim/source "orgs/kotoba-lang/aiueos/.issues/issues.edn:1 (issue F-002, security-key-lifecycle-signer-revocation); docs/issues/security-key-lifecycle-signer-revocation.md:35-44; src/aiueos/contract.cljc:248,849-850; src/aiueos/signing.cljc:244-274",
  :claim/text "aiueos's newly-added .issues/issues.edn (2026-07-26, PR #134) self-reports finding F-002 ('Security: enforce key lifecycle and signer revocation for manifests', Severity Critical) as :implemented-local, with the issue doc's own 'Local resolution evidence' section claiming a CLJC policy-level :aiueos/signer-status lifecycle vocabulary (active/retired/revoked/expired/compromised/suspended) that adapters consult to reject a revoked/expired/compromised signer. Grepping the actual current source: the exact keyword :aiueos/signer-status the issue names does not exist anywhere in src/ or test/; the only related field is contract.cljc's :aiueos.policy/signer-statuses, which is validated ONLY as a keyword-set SHAPE (a policy schema check) and never read anywhere else. aiueos.signing/verify (the actual manifest-signature verification entrypoint) checks only that a signer is registered in :aiueos.policy/signers and that the signature bytes are valid -- it never consults any signer-status field, so a manifest signed by a key the operator intends as revoked/expired/compromised still verifies exactly like one signed by an active key.",
  :claim/self-reported-level "",
  :claim/self-caveat false,
  :claim/axis [:axis/safety-enforcement :axis/doc-code-drift]}

